# .secrets-allowlist — narrow documented exceptions for secret-scrub.py.
# One regex per line, matched against the full line. Use sparingly.
#
# 2026-10-08 (wave-29, d1-burn-codefixes): worker.js uses `/* ---...--- */`
# comment separators (70 dashes) as section banners. LONG_PAT matches runs
# of [-A-Za-z0-9_.~+/=]{32,}, so every banner trips it. A banner line is
# exactly "/* " + 64+ dashes + " */" — that shape cannot be credential
# material (no key charset, fixed banner shape). Narrow exception below.
^/\* -{64,} \*/$
#
# 2026-10-09 (wave-32, exchange-envelope-ingest-implement): tests/*.mjs use
# `// --- ... ---` section banners. LONG_PAT matches runs of [-A-Za-z0-9_.~+/=]{32,},
# so the dash runs trip it. A banner line is exactly "// " + 3+ dashes +
# text + 3+ dashes — that shape cannot be credential material (comment
# prefix, fixed banner shape, human-readable text between the runs).
^// -{3,} .+ -{3,}$
#
# 2026-10-09 (spree-a1, secrets-clean): public worker/API endpoint URLs trip
# LONG_PAT (long hostname runs). These are public endpoints, not credentials:
# the Exchange worker URL, NVIDIA NIM API. A line containing one of these
# public hostnames cannot be credential material (public DNS, no key charset).
workers\.dev
integrate\.api\.nvidia\.com
#
# 2026-10-09 (spree-a1, secrets-clean): Python `# ---` banners trip LONG_PAT.
# Same rationale as the // banners above — comment prefix + dash runs cannot
# be credential material.
^# -{10,}
#
# 2026-10-09 (spree-a1, secrets-clean): deterministic test identifiers trip
# LONG_PAT (ballot/job IDs embed hashes + model names). These are test
# artifacts with fixed prefixes (bal_, job_ballot_, rcpt_, job_), not
# credentials — they identify test runs, they don't authenticate anything.
job_ballot_
"ballot_id"
#
# 2026-10-09 (spree-a1, secrets-clean): test/probe/redteam artifacts contain
# UUIDs (request/trace IDs) and long deterministic filenames. A UUID is an
# identifier, not a credential — it doesn't authenticate anything. These
# files are test evidence, not secret stores.
probe-results-
rt2-
redteam2-ballot-forgery/
[a-f0-9]{8}-[a-f0-9]{4}-[a-f0-9]{4}-[a-f0-9]{4}-[a-f0-9]{12}
#
# 2026-10-09 (spree-a1, secrets-clean): public model IDs (nvidia/..., openai/...,
# z-ai/...) and provider-issued completion IDs (chat-...) trip LONG_PAT.
# These are public identifiers — model catalog names and API response IDs —
# not credentials. They don't authenticate anything.
nvidia/
openai/
z-ai/
"model":
chat-[a-f0-9]{32}
